# TypeScript / JavaScript Security

> Origin: ECC, claude-code. On conflict, [backend.mdc](./backend.mdc) and [docs/ACCOUNTS.md](../../docs/ACCOUNTS.md) win.

## Secrets

- Never hardcode API keys, tokens, or passwords
- Worker-only: `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, D1/R2 credentials in Wrangler bindings
- App: `NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_DESKTOP`, Worker URL — **public** at build time; never put secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`

## OAuth env names

| Runtime | Client ID env |
|---|---|
| Web dev | `NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` |
| Tauri | `NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_DESKTOP` |

Rebuild `.exe` after `.env.local` changes.

## XSS

Student/teacher names and user text are untrusted. Do not use:

- `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with dynamic content
- `.innerHTML`, `.outerHTML`, `insertAdjacentHTML`
- `eval`, `new Function`, `document.write`

## Shell / subprocess

Do not use `child_process.exec` with interpolated user input; prefer `execFile` with argument arrays if Node scripts are added.

## Worker touchpoints

When editing `workers/cloud-backup`: JWT ownership for R2 prefix, body size limits, no classroom runtime logic on Worker.
